## Longs

Reference length: Europa v02 · Last Star v11 (**~7–9 min**). Open/end craft: BH v09 · AW v05 · Fermi v20 (do **not** copy their ~21-min runtimes). Next to make: **007 Neutron Star at 7–9 min**, not 18–25. Picture path: AI Studio **Veo world / Omni Orbit-only** (`OMNI_LONGFORM_PLAYBOOK.md`).

1. **First 3s = strange picture only.** No Orbit, no logo, no title, no “ORBIT / Stories from the sky”.
2. **World does the science.** Orbit in **1–2** inquisitive / story-narrative scenes only — in the scene, not a sticker. Do not force Orbit by ~8s.
3. **Leftover brand sting:** cover picture only (hold last clean frame over the sting). Audio stays uncut so the sentence finishes. Hard-cutting the sting failed BH v08 (VO chopped “Today, Or…”).
4. **After the cover,** the original next shot (chapter card, camera turn) is fine.
5. **End:** 10s last real picture. Official YouTube Studio end screens (Subscribe + next film when an id exists). No baked like/subscribe graphic or VO.
6. **Long thumb:** picture + short SEA-style hook. **No Orbit. No generic CTA.**
7. **Recut = new id.** Do not mint until Video Auditor passes after watching the open VO, not stills. Leave old live until new is public, then unpublish. Shortening a live film = new id (never swap files).
8. **No `/go/`** unless this cut names the product in VO and on screen. Shorts stay zero affiliate. JWST v04 stays film-only (no `/go/jwst-book`).
9. **Length NOW:** **7–9 min**. Later expand to 15–20–30 only with impressions + hold past ~5 min. Never chop a 21-min lecture to fake 7–9.

## Do not

- Reuse a YouTube id to swap a file.
- Score or ship from stills alone.
- Batch-dump Shorts.
- Stretch Shorts to ~60s to fit Street Dog’s six phases — Orbit Shorts stay 22–27s (DECLARE → ASSESS → REVEAL only).
- Restore the old brand sting or baked subscribe outro. Older playbook lines that say “reuse brand sting + like/subscribe outro” are wrong.
